losed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-04-01T20:50:06Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T12:53:52Z","closed_at":"2026-04-04T12:52:52Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible: Godot v4.6.1.stable, Godot v4.6.2.stable\nNot reproducible: Godot v4.5.2, Godot v4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21924.61) - AMD Ryzen 7 5700U with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 7.35 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Godot 4.6, the editor enters a state where moving any script in any project triggers a \"Cyclic Resource Inclusion\" error. This is not limited to a specific file or folder, the error message dynamically reflects the path of whichever script is being moved.\n\n**Example Error:**\nERROR: Another resource is loaded from path 'res://CurrentFolder/AnyScript.gd' (possible cyclic resource inclusion).\n\n**Key Observations:**\n\n- The issue persists even when creating brand-new projects in empty directories.\n- Deleting Godot.exe, %APPDATA%\\Godot and %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Godot and reinstalling does not resolve the state for version 4.6.\n- Versions 4.4 and 4.5 continue to function correctly on the same machine and projects\n\nThe issue was first triggered after an Autoload named _debug_ was accidentally moved via the cursor in the FileSystem dock. Since then, the 4.6 editor seems unable to correctly resolve script movements without throwing a false positive cyclic error.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n**Steps to reproduce**\n\n1. In Godot 4.6, create an Autoload named debug, and then move that script to a different folder using the cursor in the FileSystem dock.\n2. The Output console throws the \"Cyclic Resource Inclusion\" error for res://debug.gd.\n3. Create any new script (e.g., test_script.gd). Move it to any folder.\n4. Result: The Output console immediately throws the \"Cyclic Resource Inclusion\" error for res://test_script.gd and any sequential script.\n\nA least that is how it started with, difficult to redo it since this is my only computer and the problem is still happening on every project\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118088/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118088/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}